 UNIT Prolog;
 
+{ PATCH (fpc): the V- flag below relaxes fpc's strict fixed-string-length type
+  matching (Turbo Pascal treated e.g. String16/String32 as interchangeable by
+  content; fpc's default V+ requires an exact declared-length match). }
+{$V-}
+
+{ PATCH (fpc): UpdateStarArray below used two raw-8086-machine-code blocks (via the
+  Turbo Pascal Inline directive; retrace-timed direct VGA memory writes at segment
+  ScrSeg) to erase/redraw a single twinkling title-screen star -- that directive emits
+  literal machine code bytes with no fpc equivalent, categorically uncompilable under a
+  flat i386 memory model, not an fpc-strictness gap. Star is local to Prologue (the
+  title/main-menu screen) and never read outside it, so removing just those two blocks
+  (pure display, same class as this lane's other Mem[]/inline-asm removals) leaves
+  Star's Pos/Chr bookkeeping -- and everything else in this unit -- unaffected. }
+
 {$IFDEF Overlay}
 {$F+}
 {$O+}
